# Working screenshots. Only the five assets package.json and README reference
# are tracked; the rest stay local. Same allow-list shape as .vscodeignore, and
# the two lists must name the same five - they are different doors (rule 20),
# and src/release/vsix.test.ts is what checks the second one.
#
# Re-cut 2026-08-30 for the release. The three `screenshot-*.png` files were
# `0.1.x` captures of a renderer that no longer exists; they are retired into
# the private repository's `PNG Archive/` rather than deleted. What replaces
# them is four images of the shipped UI, gated before they crossed into this
# tree (`lab/docs/evidence/release-0.5.0/MEDIA-GATE.md`).
#
# `icon.png` is NOT one of the four and is not a screenshot: `package.json`
# names it as the extension icon, so removing it makes the manifest name a
# file that is not there and `vsce package` fails. It stays.
media/*
!media/icon.png
!media/Session_Deck.png
!media/hero_26_agent_session.png
!media/Internal_Session_Tool_popup.png
!media/Internal_Session_Tool_popup2.png
# The hero GIF, added for 0.6.0 (DoD 5.8). It is a SIXTH tracked image and
# not one of the four: 4,658,677 bytes, referenced by README.md, and denied
# in `.vscodeignore` so it does not ship inside the VSIX - the Marketplace
# fetches README images from the default branch of the public repository, so
# the listing renders it from GitHub rather than from the package. Different
# doors, and this one has to admit it.
!media/agent-deck-hero.gif

# The whole .claude/ directory: agent definitions, skills, working notes and
# settings.local.json. Local tooling, not product. Untracked before the public
# flip - untracking is reversible, publishing is not.
.claude/

# The maintainer's private working checkout, if they have one. It is not part
# of this project and nothing here depends on it: the suite is green without
# it, and `scripts/privacy-sweep.mjs` reports `identity=SKIPPED` rather than
# failing when it is absent. Contributors will not have one and do not need one.
lab/

# The working method and its evidence. These live in the maintainer's private
# repository and are presented back at these paths by links into `lab/`, so
# `/phase` and `/handoff` still resolve them locally while nothing here tracks
# a byte of them.
#
# `docs/` and `spike/` are directory JUNCTIONS; the five files are SYMLINKS.
# They are not hardlinks, and the distinction was measured on 2026-08-28: a
# rename-based write - `sed -i`, and most editors - severs a hardlink and
# replaces a symlink with a regular file. Either way the edit lands in a
# detached copy at this root that reads correctly and never reaches `lab/`.
# Write these paths IN PLACE.
#
# ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH, every one of them. `docs/` unanchored would
# also ignore a future `src/docs/`, and `CLAUDE.md` unanchored would ignore one
# at any depth. The recorded class is a rule shaped for one place matching
# somewhere else - it has cost this repository a shipped 38 KB mockup already,
# in the other direction.
#
# `CONTRIBUTING.md` is what a contributor reads instead, and it IS tracked.
/CLAUDE.md
/PLAN.md
/HANDOVER.md
/AGENTS.md
/agent-deck-spec.md
/docs/
/spike/

# OpenCode's per-project state directory: opencode.json, its own node_modules,
# package files. Local tooling of the engine this repo now observes - same
# treatment as .claude/. The AGENTS.md context file at the repo root is NOT
# covered by this rule: whether it is tracked is a deliberate open decision.
.opencode/

# --- The maintainer's private half (ported from release/0.5.0, 2026-08-28) ---
#
# `lab/` is the private repository holding the working method, the evidence, the
# unredacted captures and the identity set. It is OPTIONAL: nothing here depends
# on it, the suite is green without it, and `scripts/privacy-sweep.mjs` reports
# `identity=SKIPPED` rather than failing when it is absent.
#
# It was NOT ignored on this branch, and that is why this block exists. A single
# `git add -A` here would have committed `lab/identity.local.json` - the token
# set the whole scrub was run to remove - into the repository the scrub had just
# cleaned and pushed.
lab/

# The working method and its evidence, presented back at these paths by links
# into `lab/` so `/phase` and `/handoff` still resolve them locally while
# nothing here tracks a byte of them. `docs/` and `spike/` are directory
# junctions; the five files are SYMLINKS, not hardlinks - measured 2026-08-28,
# a rename-based write (`sed -i`, and most editors) severs a hardlink and
# replaces a symlink with a regular file, leaving a detached copy at this root
# that looks correct and never reaches `lab/`. Write these paths in place.
#
# ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH, every one of them. `docs/` unanchored would
# also ignore a future `src/docs/`, and `CLAUDE.md` unanchored would ignore one
# at any depth.
/CLAUDE.md
/PLAN.md
/HANDOVER.md
/AGENTS.md
/agent-deck-spec.md
/docs/
/spike/
